# CMS PHP 7.4

Live `/cms/api/ops/events.php` returned empty HTTP 500 because `cms/includes/ops-store.php` used PHP 8 syntax. Auth endpoints that only load `bootstrap.php` still worked.

Forbidden in `cms/` (parse or runtime fatal on 7.4):

- Type hints `mixed`, union types (`string|int`), `never`
- `match (...)`
- `$e::class` — use `get_class($e)`
- Nullsafe `$foo?->bar`
- Relying on `str_contains` / `str_starts_with` without the polyfills in `bootstrap.php`

Arrow functions (`fn`) and trailing commas in calls are fine (7.4). `{mixed}` in docblocks is fine.

If you add a PHP 8 helper, polyfill it at the top of `bootstrap.php` the same way as `str_contains`.
